------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party tools invoked as separate programs (NOT part of this source distribution)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

intelligent-release-image-staging distributes and stages software images — and
builds its optional IOx application packages — by INVOKING the following tools as
separate, independent programs (subprocesses). It does not link against, embed,
include, or derive from their source code. Each tool is executed via its own
command-line / RPC interface and remains under its own license:

  * aria2c   — GNU General Public License, version 2 (GPLv2).
               Provided by aria2-next (a fork of aria2), built as a
               fully-static musl binary by a separate project which pins the
               source by commit SHA and applies local patches. It is HANDED IN
               to this repository as a binary artifact, verified against
               tools/aria2c.sha256, and is NOT downloaded, NOT built, and NOT
               stored in this source repository. This applies to every build
               path that stages it — the server (see tools/get-aria2c.sh and
               server/Dockerfile) and the optional IOx application packages
               (see device/iox/build.sh, which resolves aria2c from an
               operator-supplied ARIA2C_BIN or from deliverables/aria2c-<arch>,
               checksum-verified against tools/aria2c.sha256, and fails closed
               with no network fallback if neither is available). It is
               communicated with only over its JSON-RPC interface and command
               line, as a separate independent program.

               Corresponding source (GPLv2 §3), complete and in this
               repository — nothing has to be requested: the upstream fork
               https://github.com/AnInsomniacy/aria2-next at commit
               d4971f0e12322e2ffcdb1721911b7d5c6206d0e5; the patches in
               tools/aria2c-patches/, applied in numeric order; and the
               scripts used to control compilation in tools/aria2c-build/
               (Dockerfile + build.sh). The README in each directory
               explains how to rebuild.

  * mktorrent — GNU General Public License, version 2 (GPLv2).
               Installed as a system package and invoked as a subprocess to
               create .torrent metadata.

  * openssl  — Apache License, Version 2.0 (OpenSSL 3.x).
               Installed as a system package and invoked as a subprocess
               (e.g. to generate secrets and TLS material).

  * ioxclient — Cisco IOx Client — proprietary Cisco software distributed by
               Cisco Systems, Inc. under its own license terms. It is
               operator-provided (staged at tools/bin/ioxclient or pointed to by
               the IOXCLIENT variable), which keeps IOx package builds working in
               air-gapped environments, and is invoked only as a separate
               command-line program to build the optional IRIS IOx application
               packages (iris-arm64.tar / iris-amd64.tar). It is NOT part of this
               source repository and is NOT redistributed here.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party programs installed in the distributed server image
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The published seed-server container image (server/Dockerfile) additionally
installs the following Debian system packages. They are redistributed inside
that image as separate, unmodified programs; IRIS does not link against, embed,
or derive from any of them. Each remains under its own license. Licenses are
named as the upstream projects publish them; consult each project for the
authoritative text.

  * sshpass  — GNU General Public License, version 2 (GPLv2).
               Installed as a system package and invoked as a subprocess
               (argv ["sshpass", "-e", "scp", ...]) so the audit-export upload
               and the server-side device sessions can supply an SSH password
               from the environment. Never modified, never linked.

  * age      — MIT License. Copyright (c) The age Authors.
               Installed as a system package and invoked as a subprocess to
               encrypt and decrypt the at-rest secret store (IRIS_AGE_BIN).

  * OpenSSH client (ssh, scp)
             — BSD-style OpenSSH license, with components under other
               permissive terms. Copyright (c) 1995 Tatu Ylonen and the
               OpenSSH contributors. Installed as a system package and invoked
               as a subprocess for every server-side device session and for the
               audit-export upload.

  * curl     — curl license (MIT/X derivative). Copyright (c) 1996-2026
               Daniel Stenberg and contributors. Installed as a system package;
               invoked by the image's own HEALTHCHECK.

  * ca-certificates
             — Mozilla Public License 2.0 (the CA certificate data);
               the Debian packaging scripts are under their own terms.
               Installed as a system package to supply the system trust store.

  * unzip    — Info-ZIP license (BSD-style). Copyright (c) 1990-2009
               Info-ZIP. Installed as a system package; present for operator
               convenience inside the container.

  * iproute2 — GNU General Public License, version 2. Installed as a system
               package; present for operator diagnostics inside the container.

The IOx and IOS-XR device images (device/iox/Dockerfile, device/xr/Dockerfile)
install a smaller set of the same kinds of packages under the same terms; see
those files for the exact list per image.

